Subject: leave the user runtime directory to turnstile

pam_elogind does not export XDG_RUNTIME_DIR, and elogind neither mounts a
tmpfs at /run/user/<uid> at a user's first login nor unmounts and removes
it at the last logout. turnstile (manage_rundir) creates, exports and
removes the directory instead, and keeps it for a lingering user, whose
boxes and user services would otherwise lose their sockets when elogind
removed it at logout.

Carried from Chimera Linux's elogind (cports main/elogind,
no-runtime-dir.patch, by q66), with its hunks
placed for 255.24.

